SSG Converter

Responsible for reproducing:

parameter resolution
SGS lookup
variable evaluation
conditional generation
iteration
process expansion
generated source
generated ECL

Do not automatically convert every SSG variable into a runtime PowerShell variable.

ECL Converter

Responsible for reproducing the intent of:

resource assignment
logical file binding
execution ordering
program invocation
status handling
cleanup

AMT equivalents may replace literal OS 2200 commands.

COBOL Converter

Responsible for reproducing:

record layouts
REDEFINES
numeric representation
OPEN
READ
WRITE
EOF behaviour
business calculations
record preservation
AMT Libraries

Prefer existing AMT runtime capabilities where they genuinely reproduce the required semantics.

Do not create custom emulation before checking whether AMT already provides the required facility.

16. Mandatory Copilot Rules
Rule 1

Never infer original Unisys behaviour from converted PowerShell or C#.

Rule 2

Before implementing a semantic behaviour, classify the evidence:

PROVEN_BY_UNISYS_MANUAL
OBSERVED_IN_FEDERALE_SOURCE
DERIVED_WORKING_MODEL
ASSUMPTION
UNKNOWN

Rule 3

Never invent missing Unisys behaviour.

If evidence is insufficient, write:

UNKNOWN


or:

ASSUMPTION

Rule 4

Preserve the distinction between:

SSG generation time


and:

program runtime

Rule 5

Do not model ACOB as the execution stage.

Current working model:

ACOB = compiler
MAP  = collection/link stage
XQT  = execution

Rule 6

Do not assume:

UCOB -> MAP


is mandatory.

Rule 7

Do not translate OS 2200 commands literally unless required.

Translate their semantics.

Rule 8

Validate behaviour rather than generated syntax.

Rule 9

Before creating new C#, PowerShell, or runtime emulation, search the existing AMT libraries and project assets for equivalent functionality.

Rule 10

Do not modify production converters until the reference behaviour for the selected test case is understood.

17. Mock Test Set

Create synthetic fixed-width records.

Minimum tests:

Test	PurposeBaseline	Normal record transformation
Multiple fields	Verify repeated generated overlays
Zero	Verify zero representation
Negative	Verify signed representation
Boundary width	Verify maximum field width
Invalid numeric	Verify deterministic failure
Empty file	Verify EOF behaviour
Generation variation	Change SGS parameters and verify generated model changes
Binding variation	Change physical file while keeping logical model unchanged
Invalid offset	Verify generation-time validation

Do not use production-sensitive data.

